IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-dates`
IMPORT `lsl-core`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1955 (NSW) -- THE SEAT OF THE WORKER: the employee claiming long service leave or pay for it
-- (and, where the worker has died, the personal representative claiming for the estate). Every question is asked as
-- the worker would ask it, from facts the worker can state; judgments left to a tribunal or to the parties' agreement
-- are asked as conditions. The rules are in lsl-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2024). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The questions of the worker`

-- Builds the core's record from the plain answers; every field is read by some rule.
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE
      `my last day` IS A DATE
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER
      `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended`
      `weeks already taken or paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Service facts`
`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `my last day` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `how it ended` `taken` `weeks already taken or paid` MEANS
    `Service facts` WITH
        `the day service began`       IS `the day I started`
        `the last day of service`     IS `my last day`
        `days not counted`            IS `days of breaks not counted`
        `how it ended`                IS `how it ended`
        `weeks already taken or paid` IS `weeks already taken or paid`

§§ `Am I covered?`

@export Does the NSW Long Service Leave Act 1955 give me long service leave with my employer (ss 3, 4(1), 5)?
GIVEN `how I work` IS A `How I work` @desc How you work for the other person: employed by them (on salary, wages, piecework or commission, or as an outworker or under a labour-only contract); plying for hire, delivering goods or carrying passengers in a vehicle or vessel they bail to you, in work for which an award or industrial agreement fixes a rate; deemed their employee by the Industrial Relations Act 1996; or not employed, working on your own account
      `the tribunal is satisfied the bailment is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a vehicle or vessel bailed to you: whether a tribunal hearing proceedings under the Act has been satisfied that the bailment contract was genuine and not made to avoid the Act (answer false if no tribunal has so found)
      `I am a worker under the metalliferous mining Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker under the Long Service Leave (Metalliferous Mining Industry) Act 1963
      `my award or agreement gives more favourable long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award or enterprise agreement covering your class of workers gives long service leave more favourable to you than this Act
      `another Act gives my class of workers long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act (not this one or the Industrial Relations Act 1996) provides long service leave for your class of workers
      `the exemption status` IS AN `Exemption status` @desc Whether the Industrial Relations Commission has exempted your employer's own long service scheme from the Act, and if so whether you elected in writing, within 3 months, to come under the Act instead
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`Does the Act give me long service leave` MEANS
    `the coverage answer for` `how I work` `bailment bona fide` `the tribunal is satisfied the bailment is bona fide` `metalliferous` `I am a worker under the metalliferous mining Act` `award` `my award or agreement gives more favourable long service leave` `other Act` `another Act gives my class of workers long service leave` `exemption` `the exemption status`

-- Situation: your employer runs its own long service scheme that the Industrial Relations Commission has exempted.
@export My employer's long service scheme is exempt from the Act: by when must I elect, in writing, to come under the Act instead (s 5(2)(c)(i))?
GIVEN `the day the exemption took effect` IS A DATE @desc The date from which the Industrial Relations Commission's exemption of your employer took effect
      `the day my employment began` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment with this employer began
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I elect to come under the Act` MEANS
    `the last day to elect out of an exempt scheme` `the day the exemption took effect` `the day my employment began`

§§ `My service`

-- Situation: your service had a break (an absence, a stand-down, a move, a gap between jobs).
@export Was my service with my employer continuous despite this break, and do the days of the break count (ss 4(11), 4(13), 15C)?
GIVEN `the kind of break` IS A `Kind of break` @desc What the break was: an absence under the terms of your employment (such as paid leave); an absence because of illness or injury; your employer ending or interrupting your service to avoid long service or sick leave obligations; an industrial dispute; your employer ending or interrupting it for slackness of trade; an absence with your employer's leave; your employer ending or interrupting it for another reason; you resigning or leaving and later coming back; a COVID-19 stand-down without pay; the business being transferred to a new employer with you; a move to a related corporation; or the gap after finishing an apprenticeship
      `the day it began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the break (your first day off work; after an apprenticeship or a job with a related corporation, the day after it ended)
      `the day I came back` IS A DATE @desc The day you were back at work for the employer, or began the new contract of employment
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`Was my service continuous despite this break` MEANS
    `the continuity answer for` `the kind of break` `from` `the day it began` `back on` `the day I came back`

@export On what day do I first become entitled to long service leave, after 10 years of service (s 4(2)(a)(i)(A))?
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day your service with this employer began (including service carried over from a transmitted business, a related corporation or an apprenticeship that counts)
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of breaks in your service that are not counted as service (as the continuity question works out); 0 if none
GIVETH A DATE
`When do I first become entitled to long service leave` MEANS
    `the day first entitled for` (`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `the day I started` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `it has not ended: I am still employed` `taken` 0)

§§ `How much leave`

@export How many weeks of long service leave have I earned with my employer, in total, before deducting leave already taken (s 4(2))?
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day your service with this employer began (including service carried over from a transmitted business, a related corporation or an apprenticeship that counts)
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc Your last day of employment; if you are still employed, the day you are asking about
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of breaks in your service that are not counted as service (as the continuity question works out); 0 if none
      `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc Whether and how your employment ended: still employed; moved to a related corporation; terminated by your employer, other than for serious and wilful misconduct; terminated for serious and wilful misconduct; ended by you because of illness, incapacity or domestic or other pressing necessity; ended by you for another reason; your death; or ended in another way, such as the end of a fixed term
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave have I earned` MEANS
    `the weeks of long service leave for` (`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `my last day` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `how it ended` `taken` 0)

@export How many weeks of long service leave am I still owed, after deducting leave already taken or paid for (s 4(2), (2)(b), (5))?
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day your service with this employer began (including service carried over from a transmitted business, a related corporation or an apprenticeship that counts)
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc Your last day of employment; if you are still employed, the day you are asking about
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of breaks in your service that are not counted as service (as the continuity question works out); 0 if none
      `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc Whether and how your employment ended: still employed; moved to a related corporation; terminated by your employer, other than for serious and wilful misconduct; terminated for serious and wilful misconduct; ended by you because of illness, incapacity or domestic or other pressing necessity; ended by you for another reason; your death; or ended in another way, such as the end of a fixed term
      `weeks already taken or paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave (or leave like it) already taken or paid for, for this service, including leave taken in advance; leave given under an agreement for leave on top of the Act's is not counted
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many weeks of long service leave am I still owed` MEANS
    `the weeks still owed for` (`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `my last day` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `how it ended` `taken` `weeks already taken or paid`)

@export What is my weekly ordinary pay for long service leave (s 3(1) "ordinary pay", (2), (2A), (2C))?
GIVEN `I am paid wholly at a time rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day before your leave begins (or your employment ended), you are paid wholly at an ordinary time rate fixed by your terms of employment (rather than by piecework, commission or the like)
      `my weekly ordinary remuneration now` IS A NUMBER @desc For a time-rate worker: your pay for your normal weekly hours at your time rate (the higher rate if there are several), without shift, overtime or penalty rates, in dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my average weekly ordinary remuneration over 5 years` IS A NUMBER @desc For a time-rate worker: the average weekly amount of that ordinary remuneration over the part of the last 5 years you were paid that way, in dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my average weekly wage over 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc For a worker not paid wholly at a time rate: your average weekly wage over the time actually worked in the last 12 months, without shift, overtime or penalty rates, in dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my average weekly wage over 5 years` IS A NUMBER @desc For a worker not paid wholly at a time rate: the same average over the time actually worked in the last 5 years, in dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my average weekly bonuses over 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The average weekly amount of bonuses, incentives and the like received from this employer over the last 12 months, in dollars
      `my average weekly bonuses over 5 years` IS A NUMBER @desc The same average over the last 5 years, in dollars
      `my board` IS A `Board or lodging` @desc Whether your employer provided you with board just before then: not provided; provided with a cash value fixed by your terms of employment; or provided with no value fixed
      `the fixed value of my board` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly cash value of the board fixed by your terms of employment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `my lodging` IS A `Board or lodging` @desc Whether your employer provided you with lodging just before then: not provided; provided with a cash value fixed by your terms of employment; or provided with no value fixed
      `the fixed value of my lodging` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly cash value of the lodging fixed by your terms of employment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the s 3(2C) amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual amount prescribed by the regulations for s 3(2C), in dollars: above it, bonuses are left out of ordinary pay (the regulation is not in this encoding; look it up)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my weekly ordinary pay` MEANS
    `the weekly ordinary pay for` (`Pay facts` WITH
        `paid wholly at an ordinary time rate`          IS `I am paid wholly at a time rate`
        `weekly ordinary remuneration now`              IS `my weekly ordinary remuneration now`
        `average weekly ordinary remuneration, 5 years` IS `my average weekly ordinary remuneration over 5 years`
        `average weekly wage, 12 months`                IS `my average weekly wage over 12 months`
        `average weekly wage, 5 years`                  IS `my average weekly wage over 5 years`
        `average weekly bonuses, 12 months`             IS `my average weekly bonuses over 12 months`
        `average weekly bonuses, 5 years`               IS `my average weekly bonuses over 5 years`
        `board`                                         IS `my board`
        `fixed weekly value of board`                   IS `the fixed value of my board`
        `lodging`                                       IS `my lodging`
        `fixed weekly value of lodging`                 IS `the fixed value of my lodging`
        `the s 3(2C) annual amount`                     IS `the s 3(2C) amount`)

§§ `Taking my leave`

@export Can I take my long service leave in separate periods, in advance, or from a later agreed date (s 4(3), (3AA), (3A))?
GIVEN `the way I want to take it` IS A `How I want to take the leave` @desc How you want to take the leave: in one continuous period; in two or more separate periods; in advance, before you are entitled to it; or from a later date agreed with your employer
      `my employer agrees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has agreed to that way of taking it
      `the shortest period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc The shortest single period of leave you want to take, in days (for one continuous period, its length)
GIVETH A `Taking leave answer`
`Can I take my leave this way` MEANS
    `the taking leave answer for` `the way I want to take it` `agreed` `my employer agrees` `shortest` `the shortest period in days`

-- Situation: you have no fixed normal weekly hours.
@export I have no fixed weekly hours: how many hours count as one day of long service leave (s 4(3B))?
GIVEN `my average weekly hours over 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average weekly hours worked over the 12 months ending the day before the leave begins
      `my average weekly hours over 5 years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average weekly hours worked over the 5 years ending the day before the leave begins
      `my average days a week over 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The average number of days you worked each week over those 12 months
      `my average days a week over 5 years` IS A NUMBER @desc The average number of days you worked each week over those 5 years
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours is one day of my leave` MEANS
    `the hours in a day of leave for` `my average weekly hours over 12 months` `and` `my average weekly hours over 5 years` `working` `my average days a week over 12 months` `or` `my average days a week over 5 years`

@export How many days longer is my long service leave because of public holidays falling in it (s 4(4A))?
GIVEN `public holidays in my leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many public holidays appointed by the Governor for the whole of New South Wales fall during your long service leave
      `I am entitled to payment for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to be paid for those days under an Act, award, industrial agreement or your contract of employment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many extra days do I get for public holidays` MEANS
    `the extra days for` `public holidays in my leave` `paid` `I am entitled to payment for them`

@export Did my employer give me enough notice of the day my long service leave begins (s 4(10), (10A))?
GIVEN `the day my leave begins` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer proposes that your long service leave begins
      `the day I was told` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer gave you notice of that date
      `I agreed to less notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you agreed to less than one month's notice
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`Was I given enough notice of my leave` MEANS
    `the notice answer for leave beginning` `the day my leave begins` `notified on` `the day I was told` `agreed` `I agreed to less notice`

§§ `Being paid for my leave`

@export Can I be paid for my long service leave instead of taking it, and who must be paid when my employment ends (s 4(5), (5A), (5B), (8), (9), (13)(e), s 7)?
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc Whether and how your employment ended: still employed; moved to a related corporation; terminated by your employer, other than for serious and wilful misconduct; terminated for serious and wilful misconduct; ended by you because of illness, incapacity or domestic or other pressing necessity; ended by you for another reason; your death (asked by your personal representative); or ended in another way, such as the end of a fixed term
      `I am a registered portable scheme worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a registered worker under the Building and Construction Industry Long Service Payments Act 1986 or the Contract Cleaning Industry (Portable Long Service Leave Scheme) Act 2010
      `I have applied to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to your employer for the leave or the payment
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`Can I be paid for my leave instead of taking it` MEANS
    `the payment answer for` `how it ended` `registered` `I am a registered portable scheme worker` `applied` `I have applied to my employer`

-- Situation: your employment has ended (or you ask as the personal representative of a worker who died).
@export My employment has ended: how much must my employer pay me for my untaken long service leave (s 4(2), (5)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day your service with this employer began (including service carried over from a transmitted business, a related corporation or an apprenticeship that counts)
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc Your last day of employment
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of breaks in your service that are not counted as service (as the continuity question works out); 0 if none
      `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc How your employment ended: terminated by your employer, other than for serious and wilful misconduct; terminated for serious and wilful misconduct; ended by you because of illness, incapacity or domestic or other pressing necessity; ended by you for another reason; your death; ended in another way, such as the end of a fixed term (still employed, or a move to a related corporation, gives 0)
      `weeks already taken or paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave (or leave like it) already taken or paid for, for this service, including leave taken in advance
      `my weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay as on the day before your employment ended, in dollars (as the ordinary pay question works out)
      `already paid for that leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount already paid to you for that untaken leave, in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I be paid for my untaken leave` MEANS
    `the termination payment for` (`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `my last day` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `how it ended` `taken` `weeks already taken or paid`) `at` `my weekly ordinary pay` `less` `already paid for that leave`

-- Situation: you took long service leave in advance and your employment has ended.
@export I took long service leave in advance and my employment has ended: what is the most my employer may deduct from my final pay for it (s 4(5)(c), (5AA))?
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day your service with this employer began
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc Your last day of employment
      `days of breaks not counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The total days of breaks in your service that are not counted as service; 0 if none
      `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended` @desc How your employment ended (still employed, or a move to a related corporation, gives 0)
      `weeks already taken or paid` IS A NUMBER @desc All weeks of long service leave taken or paid for, for this service, including the leave taken in advance
      `I took the leave in advance by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave was taken in advance under an agreement with your employer (s 4(3A))
      `the pay per week I received for it` IS A NUMBER @desc The ordinary pay you received for each week of the leave taken in advance, in dollars
      `my weekly ordinary pay at the end` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay as at the end of your employment, in dollars
      `my final pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The remuneration payable to you on the termination, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can be deducted for leave I took in advance` MEANS
    `the most that may be deducted for` (`my service from` `the day I started` `to` `my last day` `less` `days of breaks not counted` `ended` `how it ended` `taken` `weeks already taken or paid`) `advance` `I took the leave in advance by agreement` `paid at` `the pay per week I received for it` `now` `my weekly ordinary pay at the end` `from` `my final pay`

§§ `If I am not paid`

-- Situation: a long service leave payment due to you has not been paid.
@export By when must I apply to the Local Court or the Industrial Relations Commission to recover an unpaid long service leave payment (s 12(1), s 4(9))?
GIVEN `the day the payment became due` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment became due to you (on termination, the day your employment ended)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to recover my unpaid long service leave pay` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for a payment due on` `the day the payment became due`

@export Is my application to recover an unpaid long service leave payment within the Act's 6 years (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the day the payment became due` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment became due to you (on termination, the day your employment ended)
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already applied to the Local Court or the Industrial Relations Commission in Court Session
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (any day if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`Is my claim for unpaid long service leave pay in time` MEANS
    `the recovery answer for a payment due on` `the day the payment became due` `applied` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `as of` `today`

@export Until when must my former employer keep my long service leave record (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the day I ceased to be employed` IS A DATE @desc The day you ceased to be employed by the employer
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when must my employer keep my record` MEANS
    `the record must be kept until` `the day I ceased to be employed`

@export What penalty does my employer face for not giving or paying my long service leave, and who can take the proceedings (ss 10, 10A, 11)?
GIVEN `my employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a company or other body corporate
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`What penalty does my employer face` MEANS
    `the penalty answer for a corporate employer` `my employer is a corporation`
